# Single-origin reverse proxy. TLS is terminated by Cloudflare (the tunnel), so
# Caddy serves plain HTTP on :80 inside the Docker network.
#   /api/*  -> API server (keeps the /api prefix the server expects)
#   /*      -> frontend
#
# Cache-Control: no-store on the frontend response is deliberate, not an
# oversight - this is a live app, not a static site. Without it, a plain
# reload (the kiosk's Refresh button, or an SSE-triggered auto-reload after a
# deploy) can be served a stale copy from Cloudflare's edge cache sitting in
# front of the tunnel, or the browser's own disk cache, and neither surfaces
# any sign of it - it just quietly shows old content until someone notices a
# recent fix isn't there. Reported live on a kiosk Pi that stayed stale
# through both a manual refresh and a full device restart. The tiny bit of
# extra bandwidth from never edge/browser-caching the JS bundle is worth it
# for a kiosk that reloads at most a few times a day.
:80 {
	@api path /api/*
	handle @api {
		reverse_proxy server:3000
	}
	handle {
		header Cache-Control "no-store"
		reverse_proxy web:5173
	}
}
